# The backend Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here ends up
# inside the published image. Before this file existed the image shipped:
#
#   .env       — the rotated JWT secret, readable by anyone who can pull the
#                image or exec into the container (F-32, D6 §7.1)
#   data/*.db  — a developer's local SQLite database, including user rows and
#                bcrypt password hashes
#   .venv/     — a host virtualenv built for a different platform, which would
#                shadow the image's own site-packages
#
# The database copy also broke `alembic upgrade head`: the volume was seeded
# from the image directory, so migrations ran against a pre-existing schema.
#
# Keep this list ahead of the Dockerfile. If you add a file holding anything
# you would not publish, exclude it here first.

# Secrets — never in an image. .env.example is intentionally NOT excluded.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local database. The runtime creates and owns /app/data via a volume.
data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Host virtualenv and caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Tests are not needed to serve requests
tests/

# Build metadata
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
